  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "19. Attached Units",
    "ruleNumber": "19.03",
    "summary": "An Attached unit carries every keyword belonging to each unit it is built from, so a rule aimed at units having one of those keywords affects the Attached unit as a whole. Individual models, though, never pick up keywords held only by other models in the unit; bear in mind that attacks are aimed at units rather than models. For example, while a PSYKER LEADER model belongs to an Attached unit, the unit counts as PSYKER even if its BODYGUARD models lack that keyword, so against a weapon with [ANTI-PSYKER 4+] an unmodified wound result of 4 or more becomes a Critical Wound even when the attack goes to a model other than that LEADER.",
